        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:12#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 13",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 13,
          "component_id": "3d0dbc26-98bd-59b9-9bcd-9c534f7959fc",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1388,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:13",
          "start": 1203
        },
        "quote": "The Building Official shall determine the net floor area of the structure and shall require off-street parking as specified for the use set forth in the applicable district regulations.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:13#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 14",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 14,
          "component_id": "1612050e-3f65-517a-a8c0-859197fcac9a",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1726,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:14",
          "start": 1389
        },
        "quote": "(4) Shared Parking Provisions. In the case of mixed uses, the off-street parking and stacking spaces required shall equal the sum of the requirements of the various uses computed separately, provided all regulations governing the location of accessory off-street parking and stacking spaces in relation to the uses served are adhered to.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:14#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 15",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 15,
          "component_id": "e23d7b02-cc64-5f5a-866c-154b0ee11fa2",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1753,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:15",
          "start": 1727
        },
        "quote": "(b) Specific Requirements.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:15#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 16",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 16,
          "component_id": "c7d65824-ec11-54bd-84e4-281dea2432a8",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1885,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:16",
          "start": 1754
        },
        "quote": "(1) Open and Enclosed Parking. Accessory off-street parking and stacking spaces may be open to the sky or enclosed within a garage.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:16#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 17",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 17,
          "component_id": "469d25e8-6866-59aa-93a8-3a1c507b5f6f",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2055,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:17",
          "start": 1886
        },
        "quote": "(2) Surfacing. All off-street parking and stacking spaces, aisles and drives shall be surfaced in accordance with the standards and specifications of the City or County.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:17#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 18",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 18,
          "component_id": "5d2691a9-473f-51a4-aade-c1b2f00d5b8d",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2156,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:18",
          "start": 2056
        },
        "quote": "(3) Location. Off-street parking and stacking spaces, aisles and drives shall be located as follows:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:18#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 19",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 19,
          "component_id": "e29a13ea-9c04-5922-97fb-a9885d12600f",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2169,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:19",
          "start": 2157
        },
        "quote": "(i) General.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:19#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 20",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 20,
          "component_id": "21df2ff6-7520-52b2-8c6c-16fedff396b7",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2307,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:20",
          "start": 2170
        },
        "quote": "(A) Bicycle parking, off-street parking and stacking spaces, aisles and drives shall be located on the same zoning lot as the use served.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:20#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 21",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 21,
          "component_id": "81fdc84e-bc9f-52e8-96fc-c18796630962",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2616,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:21",
          "start": 2308
        },
        "quote": "(B) Protective curbs shall be required to be installed three feet from public sidewalks to protect pedestrians a minimum of two feet from adjacent property lines, and at other places on the parking lot as may be required by the Code Enforcement Director or the City Engineer to protect the adjacent property.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:21#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 22",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 22,
          "component_id": "632d2f74-b2cb-573b-8484-2f4717be496f",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2808,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:22",
          "start": 2617
        },
        "quote": "(C) Aisles and drives shall not be considered in determining whether off-street parking and stacking requirements have been met except in the instance of single-family dwellings and duplexes.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:22#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 23",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 23,
          "component_id": "b333918f-c7e5-5227-ab44-663349c6f39b",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3280,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:23",
          "start": 2809
        },
        "quote": "(ii) Bicycle Parking. Bicycle parking shall be located in designated areas which minimize pedestrian and vehicle conflict. Bicycle parking shall be located within 120 feet of a main building entrance in an area that is visible and well lighted. “Well lighted” means a brightness level of at least one foot-candle. Where multiple buildings exist, bicycle parking shall be distributed in a manner that serves all of the buildings in areas that are visible and well lighted.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:23#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 24",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 24,
          "component_id": "8dd32b0e-5118-52ad-9e26-2138b32de6fd",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3475,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:24",
          "start": 3281
        },
        "quote": "(4) Design. Except for single-family dwellings and duplexes, all bicycle parking, off-street parking, and stacking spaces, aisles and drives shall comply with the following prescribed standards:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:24#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 25",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 25,
          "component_id": "b3dad4e7-e3be-5692-a142-3d063b9a7b29",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3589,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:25",
          "start": 3476
        },
        "quote": "(i) Area. Vehicular parking and stacking spaces shall comply with the minimum dimensions illustrated in Figure 1.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:25#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 26",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 26,
          "component_id": "13a86585-3ce0-523b-bfd0-4f07aadc1b1e",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3602,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:26",
          "start": 3590
        },
        "quote": "(ii) Access.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:26#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 27",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 27,
          "component_id": "0748d018-401b-59fe-aef7-6f6707374e91",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 4199,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:27",
          "start": 3603
        },
        "quote": "(A) Vehicular. Each vehicular parking space shall open directly upon an aisle of such width and design as illustrated in Figure 1. The greatest aisle width shown in Figure 1 shall be provided when combining different parking space configurations on the same aisle. All off-street parking facilities shall be designed with appropriate means of vehicular access to a street or alley in a manner which will least interfere with traffic movement; and all such points of access must be approved by the Public Works Department. Aisles designed for two-way traffic shall have a minimum width of 24 feet.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:27#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 28",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 28,
          "component_id": "a2532b4a-d8f4-5ab0-935a-4ea5f9ee1146",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 4308,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:28",
          "start": 4200
        },
        "quote": "(B) Bicycle. Each bicycle parking space shall comply with the minimum dimensions as illustrated in Figure 2.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:28#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 29",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 29,
          "component_id": "a0134552-8c80-58c4-81e7-4aa1feba1dcb",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 4492,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:29",
          "start": 4309
        },
        "quote": "(iii) Exiting a Parking Facility. No off-street parking facility shall be designed in such a manner that when exiting a parking facility it would require backing into a public street.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:29#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 30",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 30,
          "component_id": "0a9c303e-6cd3-5d3c-91ce-f396f9539a71",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 4634,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:30",
          "start": 4493
        },
        "quote": "(iv) Curbing. Protective curbing shall be installed a minimum of three feet from a public sidewalk and two feet from adjacent property lines.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:30#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 31",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 31,
          "component_id": "1998b2f0-5426-5100-8484-c11ce69a9f92",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 4772,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:31",
          "start": 4635
        },
        "quote": "(v) Markings. The parking spaces in all off-street parking areas shall be visibly delineated on the surface by painted or marked stripes.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:31#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 32",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 32,
          "component_id": "9dbac9a5-3109-576b-9345-9f1274a853c4",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 4930,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:32",
          "start": 4773
        },
        "quote": "(vi) Bicycle Rack Design. Examples of approved bicycle racks are illustrated in Figure 3. Bicycle parking racks shall meet all of the following requirements:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:32#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 33",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 33,
          "component_id": "feafa81e-341f-52e2-9c4e-2cede75abb43",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 5031,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:33",
          "start": 4931
        },
        "quote": "(A) Located on paved, impervious, or approved pervious surfaces and securely anchored to the ground;",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:33#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 34",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 34,
          "component_id": "d18845c1-5f8c-5fad-9b86-d351613f73e8",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 5079,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:34",
          "start": 5032
        },
        "quote": "(B) Support the bicycle in at least two places;",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:34#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 35",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 35,
          "component_id": "8edc772c-21bc-57b3-9226-f7ac41434640",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 5142,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:35",
          "start": 5080
        },
        "quote": "(C) Enable the frame and at least one wheel to be secured; and",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:35#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 36",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 36,
          "component_id": "327c282c-2164-5b6f-b3cd-cb770b461e6a",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 5204,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:36",
          "start": 5143
        },
        "quote": "(D) Installed according to the manufacturer’s specifications.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:36#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 37",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 37,
          "component_id": "b0595b45-b717-555e-989c-a74bf52027de",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 5413,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:37",
          "start": 5205
        },
        "quote": "(vii) Public Right-of-Way. Bicycle racks may be installed on public rights-of-way where there are no setbacks and the Public Works Director has determined that interference with pedestrian traffic is minimal.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:37#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 38",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 38,
          "component_id": "850ceffa-b7da-5b18-9c18-05b4f7998b62",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 6050,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:38",
          "start": 5414
        },
        "quote": "(5) Screening. All open, off-street parking facilities containing eight or more parking spaces shall be effectively screened on each side adjoining residential property (including single-family, duplex and multiple-family) or institutional property with a continuous, view-reducing wood fence, masonry wall, compact evergreen hedge or other landscape screening material which, when planted, will constitute an immediate view-reducing barrier. Such view-reducing screen shall be at least four feet but not more than eight feet in height. The requirement for screening may be waived with written approval from the adjacent property owner.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:38#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 39",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 39,
          "component_id": "c79db52a-eaf4-58da-970f-765349bfb7b1",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 6331,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:39",
          "start": 6051
        },
        "quote": "(6) Lighting. Any lighting used to illuminate off-street parking facilities shall be directed away from residential properties and public streets in such a way as not to create a nuisance. However, in no case shall such lighting exceed three foot-candles measured at the lot line.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:39#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 40",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 40,
          "component_id": "777c67aa-fe91-503a-be05-44a3d375590a",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 6461,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:40",
          "start": 6332
        },
        "quote": "(7) Drainage. All stormwater runoff shall be collected, transported and disposed of in a manner as approved by the City Engineer.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:40#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 41",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 41,
          "component_id": "b688ae19-607f-5afa-a604-186cfe679987",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 6705,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:41",
          "start": 6462
        },
        "quote": "(8) Accessible Parking. Where a use is required to provide accessibility for persons with disabilities, the required parking spaces shall be located and designed in accordance with standards as set by the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA).",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:41#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 42",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 42,
          "component_id": "88f5467b-b6ca-5be3-b55a-f90e45b2523d",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 7254,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:42",
          "start": 6706
        },
        "quote": "(9) Bicycle Parking. New off-street parking constructed after June 1, 2014, shall include additional parking for bicycles. The additional parking area shall be equivalent to five percent of the number of vehicular parking spaces required in TMC 18.240.030 , with a minimum of two. Parking facilities that are expanded after June 1, 2014, shall include additional parking for bicycles in the expanded area that is equal to five percent of the number of vehicular parking spaces required in TMC 18.240.030 in the expanded area, with a minimum of two.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:42#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 43",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 43,
          "component_id": "0525252b-a427-5a21-a120-ab735e8fe3fb",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 7297,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:43",
          "start": 7255
        },
        "quote": "(10) Modification of Parking Requirements.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:43#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 44",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 44,
          "component_id": "042486bb-0cd7-5d9c-b252-c2633816277c",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 8246,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:44",
          "start": 7298
        },
        "quote": "(i) Reduction of Parking Spaces. Where it can be demonstrated by the property owner that a specific use has such characteristics that the number of parking or stacking spaces required is too restrictive, the Planning Director may, upon request, grant up to a 25 percent reduction in the number of required spaces. Such request shall be filed with the Planning Director on forms as may be provided. Should a reduction greater than 25 percent be requested, the applicant may request a variance from the Board of Zoning Appeals in accordance with the procedures set forth in Chapter 2.220 TMC. Where a reduction of 25 percent or less is requested, the applicant shall be required to reserve an area of land on the site of the use served equal in size to the area of land needed to provide the spaces for which a reduction is granted. Such land reserved shall be suitable for development of a parking facility and conform with the parking requirements.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:44#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 45",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 45,
          "component_id": "d7414ec1-e19f-5598-8ae2-cc476a51ce84",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 8490,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:45",
          "start": 8247
        },
        "quote": "(ii) Bicycle Parking Substitution. In addition to the bicycle parking required in subsection (b)(9) of this section, up to 10 percent of the number of vehicular parking spaces required in TMC 18.240.030 may be substituted with bicycle parking.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:45#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 46",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 46,
          "component_id": "f3258e36-cedb-5483-b57b-1f70827fc873",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 8894,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:46",
          "start": 8491
        },
        "quote": "(11) Condition of Off-Street Parking Facility. Any parking facility which does not meet the standards of this division and which shall create a nuisance to the public from any cause shall meet the requirements as recommended by the City or County Traffic Engineer, City or County Engineer, Planning Director and City or County Building Official, pertaining to screening, surfacing or entrances or exits.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:46#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.240.020 block 47",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 47,
          "component_id": "0d2cd354-276d-567a-9eda-d251382fefa8",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 8903,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:47",
          "start": 8895
        },
        "quote": "FIGURE 1",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.240.020:block:47#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
